     $ sqlite-utils insert dogs.db dogs dogs.json --truncate
 
+Transforming data while inserting
+----------------------------------
+
+The ``--convert`` option can run a snippet of Python against each incoming
+object before it is inserted. The object is available as ``row`` and can be
+modified in place. For example, this increments ``n`` and converts it from a
+string to an integer::
+
+    $ sqlite-utils insert data.db numbers numbers.json \
+        --convert 'row["n"] = int(row["n"]) + 1'
+
+Every input object is preserved and inserted after the conversion has run.
+This also works with newline-delimited JSON, including data piped to standard
+input::
+
+    $ cat numbers.jsonl | sqlite-utils insert data.db numbers - --nl \
+        --convert 'row["n"] = int(row["n"]) + 1'
+
